    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d530">

                <pb facs="0656" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg554"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Wilson to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-03-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 316.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the department’s cablegram of
                    March 19, I have the honor to report that until this time the British legation
                    at Brussels has received no instructions of the kind referred to therein.</p>
                <p>Should the British minister submit any propositions for a concerted action to me,
                    I will immediately cable them fully.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
